.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQKFEINI 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqkfeini ,
.Nm nqkfeupd ,
.Nm nqkfefin ,
.Nm nqkfdini ,
.Nm nqkfdupd ,
.Nm nqkfdfin
.Nd seal a stream to an ML-KEM public key, chunk by chunk
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqkfeini
.Fa "nqkfctx *c" "nqkalg alg" "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "uint32_t chunk"
.Fa "uint8_t *hdr" "size_t cap" "size_t *hlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkfeupd
.Fa "nqkfctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkfefin
.Fa "nqkfctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkfdini
.Fa "nqkfctx *c" "nqkalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *hdr" "size_t hlen" "uint32_t *chunk"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkfdupd
.Fa "nqkfctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkfdfin
.Fa "nqkfctx *c" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions write and read noqtis-kstream-1, a stream sealed to an
ML-KEM public key in chunks (the STREAM construction of Hoang,
Reyhanitabar, Rogaway and Vizar on ChaCha20-Poly1305), so that a file
of any size is encrypted and checked in the memory of one chunk.
.Pp
The header is
.Dv NQKFHDR
(17) bytes and the ML-KEM ciphertext:
.Li NQKF ,
the version 1, the algorithm (one byte, its
.Vt nqkalg ) ,
the chunk size (32 bits, big-endian) and a random 7-byte nonce prefix.
The key is HKDF-SHA-256 of the shared secret, with info
.Li noqtis-kstream-1 ,
the SHA3-256 of the public key, the context's length (one byte) and
bytes, and the whole header: a changed header gives another key and
the first tag fails.
Chunk
.Va i
is its plaintext under ChaCha20-Poly1305 and a 16-byte tag, with the
nonce prefix,
.Va i
(32 bits, big-endian) and a byte that is 1 for the last chunk and 0
before it.
Every chunk but the last holds exactly the chunk size; the last holds 0
to the chunk size, so an empty stream is one empty last chunk.
.Pp
.Fn nqkfeini
writes the header to
.Fa hdr ;
.Fn nqkfeupd
seals one full chunk and
.Fn nqkfefin
the last, each to
.Fa out
with its tag.
.Fn nqkfdini
reads the header
.Fa ( hlen
exactly 17 plus the KEM ciphertext's size) and gives the chunk size;
.Fn nqkfdupd
opens a chunk of the chunk size plus 16 bytes and
.Fn nqkfdfin
the last, which the caller knows as the one the input ends with.
Plaintext reaches
.Fa out
only when the chunk's tag verifies.
The chunk size is
.Dv NQKFCMIN
(1024) to
.Dv NQKFCMAX
(16 MiB), 0 for
.Dv NQKFCHUNK
(64 KiB); a header with another is refused
.Pq Er NQELIM
before anything is derived.
At most 2^32 chunks: the next would repeat a nonce
.Pq Er NQELIM .
The last call, and any error but
.Er NQEBUF ,
ends the stream: the context is wiped and then gives
.Er NQESTATE .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A
.Dv NULL
pointer, a context over 255 bytes, a chunk size out of range for
.Fn nqkfeini ,
or a piece of the wrong size to seal.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small;
.Pf * Fa hlen
or
.Pf * Fa outlen
gets the size needed.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
A key of the wrong length, a header that is not noqtis-kstream-1 for
.Fa alg ,
or a chunk of the wrong size to open.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
A chunk size out of range in a header, or the chunk counter's end.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
A chunk's tag does not verify;
.Fa out
is zeroed.
.It Bq Er NQESTATE
The context is not open in this direction.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fa alg
is HQC.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-box 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1 ,
.Xr nqkseal 3
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 203, RFC 5869, RFC 8439.
